  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Brown eggplant: Cut the eggplants into 2cm chunks (see Kitchen tip). Heat 2 tbs olive oil in a large deep frypan over medium-high heat. Cook the eggplant, covered, stirring occasionally, for 8 mins or until softened.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/140778/photos/large/brown_eggplant-2b73e026bef20302706fedbb5852e520.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Meanwhile, thinly slice 2 garlic cloves. Cut the olives in half. Coarsely chop the parsley, including the stems. Put the almonds in a cold small frypan over medium heat. Toast, tossing, for 3-4 mins until evenly golden.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/140779/photos/large/prep_ingredients-3ff87bc8937f327f77b2c0a9d4f0eea7.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer eggplant: Add the garlic to the eggplant mixture and cook, stirring, for 2 mins. Add the tomatoes, 1 tbs tomato paste, 1 tsp sugar, 1 tsp red wine vinegar and 2 tbs water. Cook, covered, stirring occasionally, for 10 mins or until thickened. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/140780/photos/large/simmer_eggplant-169692b41fa97e3f0836ca601d97516a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook couscous: Meanwhile, put the couscous in a large heatproof bowl, pour over 180ml (¾ cup) boiling water and cover with a plate. Stand for 5-7 mins until the water is absorbed. Fluff the grains with a fork.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/140781/photos/large/cook_couscous-4e232fdfaa86ca1e9196db4de3862f51.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Add the capers, olives and half the parsley to the eggplant and stir to combine. Divide the couscous and Sicilian eggplant among bowls. Scatter over the almonds and remaining parsley and enjoy.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/140782/photos/large/serve_up-21e2a17ad75d1b78e5b01406bdd54be0.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen tip: Only 600g (7 cups) eggplant is needed for this recipe, so if your eggplants look very large, you may want to check this. Either weigh them or fill a measuring jug with the chopped eggplant for a quick way to measure.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/140783/photos/large/kitchen_tip-e4aaf3083770df1ad96a3dacd0fd632b.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
